    "lawCode": "Amd §374, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1218A\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to the appointment for\nagricultural representation on the state fire prevention and building\ncode council\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would require that one member, appointed by the governor, to\nthe state fire prevention and building council shall be from an agricul-\ntural organization in New York State.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision 1 of section 374 of the executive law to\nadd a new paragraph (d.) to require that one member, to be appointed by\nthe governor, of the state fire prevention and building code council\nshall be from the state's largest agricultural advocacy organization.\n\nSection 2 establishes the Effective Date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChanges to the NYS Uniform Fire Prevention and Building Code have a\nsignificant impact on the agricultural community. These changes are\ndecided by the State Fire Prevention and Building Code Council, and\ncurrently there is no representation for NYS Agriculture on the council.\nThis bill would require that one member of the state fire prevention\ncouncil. and building code council shall be from an agricultural advoca-\ncy organization in New York State. This member is to be appointed by the\ngovernor.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS7115 of 2022: Passed Assembly, died in Senate\n\nA.9940 of 2020:  Referred to Government Operations.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
